rota lap 5187, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; cut and stop. Standfast and reds-first chose the lap: one booked red stood in my own lane, so no constructive work opened beside it.
think Read the card whole. Sixteen OPEN rows, seven wanting Keaton's word, and one booked red written by this ship last lap -- REDS %796, the ledger consistency guard reading a quoted noun phrase as a closure claim. Agent-doable, specified, and reddening a rostered guard on every ship at every open.
think Checked the claim board before building, per the baton's booked-red clause seated today. Five live claims, none touching the scan; opened incense-closing-line-noun-phrase and pushed it before the first edit.
think The specified exclusion -- closing touching line, sentence, word or paragraph -- freed %792 and left contradicted_rows=1. The survivor was %796 itself: the row that books the fault narrates it, so one sentence later it writes the verb beside the row it is defending.
think Measured before seating the second exclusion rather than after. Across the whole spine, 55 closure claims stand over 716 rows and exactly one carries the bold OPEN marker inside its window -- the false one. A row asserting a peer is open is the opposite of a row claiming to have closed it, which is the principle the measurement then checked.
obs The first exclusion is grammatical, the second is about who is speaking. Both are narrow and both were proven from two sides; the honest limit -- a genuine closure quoting its peer as OPEN in the same sixty characters -- is named in the scan header, the row and the card rather than left for a later reader to find.
obs Every new control leg is quoted by name in the witness. Grass booked the class this lap: a leg no witness names can flip from ok to RED while every gate stays green.
